Here is how you can do it:

```typescript
class Foo {
  ReactProperties: {
    a: string;
  }
}

type FooProperties = Foo['ReactProperties'];

console.log(FooProperties);  // Output: type { a: string; }
```

In this example, `Foo['ReactProperties']` is used to get the type of the `ReactProperties` property from the `Foo` class. 

Alternatively, if you want to do this in a generic way, you can use a type query:

```typescript
class Foo {
  ReactProperties: {
    a: string;
  }
}

type GetPropertyType<T, K extends keyof T> = T[K];

type FooProperties = GetPropertyType<Foo, 'ReactProperties'>;

console.log(FooProperties);  // Output: type { a: string; }
```

