    // Use NEON instructions
    NativeNatives ne = new NativeNatives();
    ne.nativeFunction();
}
```

### 5. Measuring Performance

Before you start optimizing your application, it's essential to measure its current performance. You can use tools like Android Studio's CPU Profiler or a library like Android Debug Bridge (ADB) to capture CPU utilization data.

```bash
adb shell dumpsys cpuinfo
```

### 6. Using A Hardware Accelerator

If your application is CPU-bound, a hardware accelerator can greatly improve its performance. A hardware accelerator like a GPU or a specialized accelerator chip can perform certain computations much faster than a CPU.

```java
