Here's a recursive function in JavaScript that retries a request 3 times before resolving the promise:

```javascript
function retryRequest(func, ...args) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    func(...args).then(
      (result) => {
        resolve(result);
      },
      (error) => {
        if (error.retryCount < 3) {
          func(...args).then(
            (result) => {
              resolve(result);
            },
            (error) => {
              error.retryCount = error.retryCount == null ? 1 : error.retryCount + 1;
              retryRequest(func, ...args, { retryCount: error.retryCount });
            }
          );
        } else {
          reject(error);
        }
      }
    );
  });
}
```

Here's an example use case for the function:

